# SQL migration files must be byte-identical on every checkout platform:
# their SHA256 checksum is load-bearing (docs/design/03-v1-alpha-foundation.md
# V1-04's tamper detection — internal/adapters/sqlite/migrations.go computes
# it from the embedded file bytes). Line-ending normalization on checkout
# would silently change that checksum per-platform, so it must never apply
# here regardless of a contributor's or CI runner's core.autocrlf setting.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Golden JSON fixtures (e.g. internal/app/doctor/testdata/golden/*.json)
# are compared byte-for-byte against freshly json.MarshalIndent-ed output,
# which always emits LF only. Without this, a Windows checkout normalizes
# these to CRLF while Linux keeps LF, making the exact same golden test
# pass on one CI OS and fail on the other for a reason that has nothing to
# do with the code under test (V1-11 hit this for real on windows-latest —
# same root cause as the *.sql rule above).
*.json text eol=lf

# Same root cause, same fix, for a non-JSON golden wire-format fixture:
# internal/delivery/httpapi/testdata/golden/sse_message_v1.txt is compared
# byte-for-byte against httpapi.WriteSSE's own output, which always emits
# LF-only "id:\nevent:\ndata:\n\n" lines (V6-02A hit this for real on
# windows-latest CI, same failure V1-11 already hit for *.json above —
# this repo currently has no other tracked *.txt file, so the pattern is
# scoped this broadly deliberately, matching the existing *.json rule's
# own scope).
*.txt text eol=lf

# Same root cause, same fix, again: web/src/api/generated.ts is compared
# byte-for-byte against apicontract.GenerateTypeScriptClient's own output
# (internal/delivery/httpapi/apicontract/tsclient_golden_test.go), which
# always emits LF only. *.tsx is included for the same reason preemptively
# (the whole web/ source tree should not have platform-dependent line
# endings once any tool — a future lint/format/snapshot check — starts
# comparing its bytes), even though nothing golden-tests a *.tsx file's
# exact bytes yet.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
